# _redirects — Cloudflare Pages
#
# Internal/attack paths are NOT blocked from this file. Cloudflare Pages
# `_redirects` only supports 200 rewrites and 3xx redirects, so a bare
# `<path> 404` rule is unsupported: Cloudflare parses `404` as a destination
# (defaulting to a 302) or drops the malformed rule, so it never returns a
# real 404. (Confirmed in production: `/test-results/*.json` stayed HTTP 200
# despite a `/test-results/* 404` rule.)
#
# Internal drafts are blocked at the source instead: `scripts/
# build_public_site.py` writes only the public tree to `dist/`, and that is
# what gets published, so those files are simply absent (a natural 404). The
# origin (Vercel) serves `dist/`; `vercel.json` additionally sets
# `X-Robots-Tag: noindex` on the same path patterns, and `robots.txt`
# disallows them for crawlers. Unknown probe paths (wp-*, *.php, dotfiles)
# are not files in `dist/` and there is no SPA catch-all, so they already
# 404 on their own. If this site is ever published as a Cloudflare Pages
# project, deploy that same `dist/` output (or add a Pages Function that
# returns 404) — do not reintroduce `<path> 404` rules here.
#
# Only rules Cloudflare Pages actually supports belong below.

# Legacy MeishiBridge support URL (also handled by vercel.json on the origin).
/meishibridge /meishi-scanner/ 301
/meishibridge/ /meishi-scanner/ 301
